{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"depilatory-bairnly-silverfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## What\n\nWrite `docs/adr/0101-*.md` amending ADR 0043. ADR 0043 itself is NOT edited — it is a historical\nrecord, and ADR 0061 already set the precedent of amending it rather than rewriting.\n\n## Must record\n\n- Why `operator` mis-signalled: it means a human throughout this repo, so agents inferred a\n  person was required, when an agent recording a Gerrit vote attests equally well.\n- Why `[non-codebase]`: it is the missing half of a pair the vocabulary already had (`[codebase]`\n  is recognized in ADR-0043 and both classification prompts), and it resists attestation\n  laundering by construction.\n- Why `attested` alone was rejected: `SOURCE_ATTESTED = \"attested\"` is the snapshot gate\n  read-root mode meaning \"pinned to an immutable in-repo SHA\" — near-opposite sense, same\n  readers, though no functional conflict.\n- That `[operator-attested]` remains accepted and is deliberately UNDOCUMENTED, because 827 of\n  4,285 live tickets carry it in immutable event records.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] ADR 0101 exists, is Accepted, and records the four points above.\n- [ ] ADR 0043 is unmodified.\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py` run; `docs/adr/README.md` and `docs/adr/.numbers/` updated.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` and `scripts/check_docs_index.py` pass.","id":"d1fb-cdeb-f3cf-4cd9","parent_id":"6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S8 — ADR 0101 amending ADR 0043 to record the rename and the retained alias"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787186022296521001,"uuid":"09ea2795-f83c-40f8-9fbd-98aedb942830"}